        "title": "Glue O and R together",
        "body": "Treat \"OR\" as a single block. Together with A, C, T this gives $4$ objects, which can be arranged in $4!=24$ ways. The block itself can be \"OR\" or \"RO\": $2$ ways. Total $2\\cdot24=48$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 48**"
