    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Did you know ... $2! = 2 \\times 1 = 2$, $3! = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6$, $4! = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24$ ?\n\nThis means that the value of $\\dfrac{11! - 9!}{11! + 9!}$ is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac{109}{111}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac{56}{65}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac{25}{26}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac{138}{137}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac{150}{151}$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factor out 9!",
        "body": "$11!=11\\cdot10\\cdot9!=110\\cdot9!$. Hence $$\\frac{11!-9!}{11!+9!}=\\frac{(110-1)\\,9!}{(110+1)\\,9!}=\\frac{109}{111}.$$\n\n**Answer: (A) $\\frac{109}{111}$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "arithmetic",
      "fractions-decimals"
    ],
