    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A jug was 60% full of water. After 20% of that water is removed the jug contains 192 ml. The maximum amount of water (in ml) that the jug could contain is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "275"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "300"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "325"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "350"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "400"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Work with the capacity",
        "body": "Let the capacity be $x$ ml. After removing 20% of the water, 80% of the water remains: $0.8\\times0.6\\,x=0.48x=192$, so $x=400$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 400**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Work backwards",
        "body": "$192$ ml is $80\\%$ of the original water, so the original water was $192\\div0.8=240$ ml. That is $60\\%$ of the capacity, so the capacity is $240\\div0.6=400$ ml.\n\n**Answer: (E) 400**"
      }
    ],
