    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the given diagram, the number in any box is equal to the sum of the numbers in the two boxes immediately below it. The value of $A$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2010-r1/q11.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "88"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "67"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "21"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "97"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "12"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Introduce a variable",
        "body": "Let the second box in the bottom row be $x$. The middle box of the second row from the bottom is $21=x+y$ where $y$ is the third bottom box, so $y=21-x$. Then the row above is $10+x$, $21$, $(21-x)+15=36-x$, the next row is $(10+x)+21=31+x$ and $21+(36-x)=57-x$, and $A=(31+x)+(57-x)=88$. The unknown cancels.\n\n**Answer: (A) 88**"
      }
    ],
