    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A car takes 2 hours to travel from Apetown to Beeville. If its speed is reduced by 30 km/h, it will take 3,2 hours. The distance from Apetown to Beeville (in km) is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "30"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "90"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "120"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "140"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "160"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Using the speed",
        "body": "Let the usual speed be $v$ km/h. Then $2v=3.2(v-30)$, so $1.2v=96$, $v=80$ and the distance is $2\\cdot80=160$ km.\n\n**Answer: (E) 160**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Using the distance",
        "body": "With distance $d$ the speeds are $\\frac d2$ and $\\frac d{3.2}$, which differ by $30$: $\\frac d2-\\frac d{3.2}=30$. Since $\\frac12-\\frac1{3.2}=0.5-0.3125=\\frac3{16}$, we get $d=30\\cdot\\frac{16}{3}=160$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 160**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "rates",
      "algebra"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
