    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the figure, $AB = 8$ cm, $AC = 10$ cm, $BD = 3$ cm, $CD = 7$ cm and $BC = 2x + 1$ cm. If $x$ is an integer, the sum of the possible values of $x$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2010-r1/q15.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Triangle inequality twice",
        "body": "In triangle $ABC$: $10-8<BC<10+8$. In triangle $BCD$: $7-3<BC<7+3$, i.e. $4<BC<10$. Both together give $4<2x+1<10$, so $1.5<x<4.5$ and $x\\in\\{2,3,4\\}$. The sum is $9$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 9**"
      }
    ],
