    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Identical matchsticks are used to make the different figures shown. 4 matchsticks make figure 1, 10 matchsticks make figure 2, 18 matchsticks make figure 3, 28 matchsticks would make figure 4, and so on. The number of matchsticks required to make figure 20 is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2010-r1/q16.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "420"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "440"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "460"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "480"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "500"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find the pattern",
        "body": "$4=1\\cdot4$, $10=2\\cdot5$, $18=3\\cdot6$, $28=4\\cdot7$. So figure $n$ needs $n(n+3)$ matchsticks. For $n=20$: $20\\cdot23=460$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 460**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Add the differences",
        "body": "Going from one figure to the next adds $6, 8, 10,\\dots$ matchsticks (figure $n+1$ adds $2n+4$). So figure $20$ has $4+\\sum_{n=1}^{19}(2n+4)=4+2\\cdot190+76=460$ matchsticks.\n\n**Answer: (C) 460**"
      }
    ],
