    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$ABCD$ and $BJKL$ are two identical squares with sides of length 8 cm. $M$ is the midpoint of $AD$ and also of $JK$. The area of the hexagon $BCDMKL$ (in cm$^2$) is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2010-r1/q18.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "64"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "80"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "96"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "112"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "128"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Union minus overlap",
        "body": "The hexagon is the union of the two squares: area $128-$ overlap. The overlap consists of triangle $ABM$ (legs $AB=8$, $AM=4$, area $16$) and triangle $BJM$ (legs $BJ=8$, $JM=4$, area $16$), which are congruent and share $BM$. The overlap is $32$, so the hexagon has area $128-32=96$ cm$^2$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 96**"
      }
    ],
