        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac p5+10$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac p{11}+10$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac p6+10$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Centre on the middle number",
        "body": "Let the middle number be $m$; the numbers are $m-10, m-8,\\dots,m+8,m+10$ and they pair up around $m$, so the sum is $11m=p$ and $m=\\frac p{11}$. The largest is $m+10=\\frac p{11}+10$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $\\frac{p}{11}+10$**"
      }
