        "key": "D",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "4"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Two cases",
        "body": "Barbara and Catherine contradict each other's claims about each other: exactly one of them is lying. \n\n- If Barbara lies, then Anne (who says Barbara is lying) tells the truth, so Diane is lying. Liars: Barbara and Diane.\n- If Catherine lies, Barbara tells the truth, so Anne is lying, and then Diane is truthful. Liars: Catherine and Anne.\n\nEither way exactly $2$ girls are lying.\n\n**Answer: (C) 2**"
      }
    ],
